2. Third-party material adapted in this repository

src/aeroscout_mission/include/aeroscout_mission/direct_waypoint_trajectory_executor.hpp
  Adapted from px4_ros2_cpp/include/px4_ros2/mission/trajectory/multicopter/
  waypoint_trajectory_executor.hpp and the matching source file of
  px4-ros2-interface-lib at 365dd8807869fd81813de0415ec99e85ea021d59.
  Modified: publishes trajectory setpoints instead of goto setpoints and is
  header-only.
  License:   BSD-3-Clause
  Copyright: Copyright (c) 2024 PX4 Development Team.

src/aeroscout_mission/include/aeroscout_mission/hover_action.hpp
  Adapted from class Hold in
  px4_ros2_cpp/include/px4_ros2/mission/actions/default_actions.hpp of
  px4-ros2-interface-lib at 365dd8807869fd81813de0415ec99e85ea021d59.
  Modified: holds position with trajectory setpoints inside the mission mode
  instead of switching to the loiter mode.
  License:   BSD-3-Clause
  Copyright: Copyright (c) 2024 PX4 Development Team.

src/aeroscout_mission/config/px4/pub.csv and sub.csv
  Derived from src/modules/zenoh/dds_topics.yaml of PX4-Autopilot at
  c72793619ee7b0a1b08458e6cccababfffc9d8ad: the topic lists rewritten as
  topic;type;instance rows with a robot namespace prefix, and one topic added.
  License:   BSD-3-Clause
  Copyright: Copyright (c) 2012 - 2025, PX4 Development Team

src/terrascout_navigation/config/navigate_to_pose.xml
  Based on nav2_bt_navigator/behavior_trees/
  navigate_w_recovery_and_replanning_only_if_path_becomes_invalid.xml of
  Navigation2 1.3.13 (https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2).
  Modified: fewer retries, node names changed or removed, error code ports
  added to the BackUp and Spin actions, and the recovery order changed.
  License:   Apache-2.0
  Copyright: the Navigation2 contributors

src/terrascout_description/urdf/scout.urdf.xacro
  The wheel mass of 2.637 kg is taken from husky_description/urdf/
  wheel.urdf.xacro of Clearpath Robotics Husky
  (https://github.com/husky/husky).
  License:   BSD-3-Clause
  Copyright: Copyright (c) 2015, Clearpath Robotics, Inc., All rights reserved.


